# Project rules

A Vue 3 component library — a schema-driven data shell. Published to npm; it has
no runtime dependencies, only peers (vue ^3.4, vue-router, optionally @nuxt/kit).

## Stack

- Vue 3 Composition API, `<script setup lang="ts">` only. Never the Options API.
- TypeScript throughout. Type props with the generic form —
  `defineProps<{ views?: ViewKind[] }>()` — never the runtime object form.
- Shared state goes in `src/composables/` and is consumed through
  `useShellContext()`, not passed down through long prop chains.

## Conventions

- Comments explain *why*, in full sentences, not what the next line does.
  Match the density of the file you are editing.
- Reuse the types in `src/types.ts` and the tokens in `src/style/tokens.css`.
  Do not invent a parallel type or hardcode a colour.
- No new runtime dependencies. If you think you need one, say so instead of
  adding it to package.json.

## Before you finish

Run these and fix what they report — do not report the work done until they pass:

    npm run lint
    npm run typecheck
    npm run test:unit

`npm run test:e2e` drives Playwright against Storybook and is slow; run it only
when asked, or when the change touches component behaviour.

## Editing

- Prefer small, targeted edits to whole-file rewrites.
- Read a file before you change it. Do not guess at an API that is one grep away.
